",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl font-bold mb-2 text-white\",\"children\":\"Research methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-8\",\"children\":\"How OpenA2A research works. Authorship, data streams, taxonomy, evidence standards, limits, citation, and how to challenge a finding.\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Authorship\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":[\"ARIA is OpenA2A's autonomous research system.\",\" \",\"Seven specialized agents handle hypothesis generation, exposure research, behavioral threat intelligence, exploit development, patch development, statistics for the indices and reports, and disclosure management.\",\" Reports authored by ARIA carry a system byline. Editorial review is done by a named human, currently Abdel Fane. Bylines on every report disclose both.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":\"Disclosure of authorship is a credibility move, not a limitation. We document how our content is made. Trust signals in 2026 favor organizations that show the work, not organizations that hide automation.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300\",\"children\":\"All findings are reviewed by a human editor before publication. The editor can return a draft for revision. The editor cannot rewrite an ARIA finding under a different byline.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Four data streams\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"OpenA2A operates four telemetry streams. Each measures a distinct slice of AI agent security. The monthly Behavioral Threat Report synthesizes across all four; specialty reports may use only one. Every stream is documented in full at its own sub-page. The newest edition is\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-10\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Issue 6 of the Behavioral Threat Report\"}],\", the 30 days ending October 17, 2026; the edition before it is\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-09\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Issue 5\"}],\", the 30 days ending September 17, 2026.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/methodology#ariascout-exposure-sweep\",\"className\":\"hover:text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"ARIAscout. Exposure sweeps.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":[\"Monthly Shodan sweeps of AI service exposure. As of\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-11-01\",\"children\":\"Nov 1, 2026\"}],\", \",\"257,625\",\" internet-facing AI services indexed. The longest-running stream. Provides the denominator for exposure prevalence comparisons. Full methodology in the ARIAscout subsection below.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/methodology/behavioral-sweep\",\"className\":\"hover:text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"ARIAtrap. Honey-agent fleet.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":\"TrapMyAgent runs 22 honey agents across sector verticals. Each agent looks like a deployed production agent to a visitor; each is instrumented to observe attacker behavior post-credential. AgentPwn instruments honeypot pages with injection payloads that an attacker-controlled agent can encounter and follow. Together they form the behavioral telemetry layer that public-web crawler studies cannot produce.\"}]]}],\"$L16\",\"$L17\"]}]]}],\"$L18\",\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\",\"$L21\",\"$L22\"]}]}],null,\"$L23\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"children\":\"$L25\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$27\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L28\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3-wliyvx6h-mw.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\ne:[\"$\",\"link\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1c_7pr18rsksy.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"34:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/2corl6wyj4669.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\na:C\n11:[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1tivn9\",{\"d\":\"M7 7h10v10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1vkiza\",{\"d\":\"M7 17 17 7\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sr-only\",\"children\":\" (external site)\"}]\n13:[\"$\",\"li\",\"https://github.com/opena2a-org/hackmyagent\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/opena2a-org/hackmyagent\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 text-gray-300 transition-colors hover:text-teal-200\",\"children\":[\"HackMyAgent\",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1tivn9\",{\"d\":\"M7 7h10v10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1vkiza\",{\"d\":\"M7 17 17 7\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sr-only\",\"children\":\" (external site)\"}]]}]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-10 text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-gray-400\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-plex-mono), monospace\"},\"children\":[\"OpenA2A Research. Questions about a report:\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:[email withheld by Lighthouse]\",\"className\":\"text-gray-300 underline-offset-2 hover:text-teal-200 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"[email withheld by Lighthouse]\"}]]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-[12px] leading-relaxed\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"var(--font-plex-mono), monospace\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://opena2a.org/privacy\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-0.5 text-gray-300 transition-colors hover:text-teal-200\",\"children\":[\"Privacy\",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0\",\"aria-hidden\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1tivn9\",{\"d\":\"M7 7h10v10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1vkiza\",{\"d\":\"M7 17 17 7\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sr-only\",\"children\":\" (external site)\"}]]}]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":\"HoneyMap. Wild bait sampling.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":\"Samples the public web through CommonCrawl, Shodan banner data, and CT-log domain expansion for adversarial injection payloads planted by third parties. HoneyMap reports aggregate counts and a signature leaderboard. HoneyMap findings are a sample of the public web, not a coverage count of every site online. The HoneyMap stream is currently published under research.opena2a.org until the brand reaches independent publication scale.\"}]]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/methodology/foitw\",\"className\":\"hover:text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"First Observed In The Wild (FOITW).\"}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":\"Pre-registered signatures for sophisticated AI agent attack techniques. When research publishes a new technique class, we register a signature in our pre-registration catalog and watch the honeypot fleet for first wild observation. Publication SLA is within seven days of first observed firing. Registration timestamps are commits in the catalog repository. Transparency-log anchoring of those timestamps is not yet implemented.\"}]]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-sem"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Registry trust signals (opt-in)\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":\"Where deployed scanners (HMA), guards (ARP), verifiers (AIM), and brokers (Secretless) are opted in, telemetry from those deployments contributes supplementary signal. Examples include scan volume, check failure rates, trust score distribution, and capability decision counts. All Registry telemetry is opt-in. Reports cite Registry signals only when the deploying organization has explicitly authorized inclusion in research data.\"}]]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Deduplication rule\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":\"One number, one home. Each metric lives in exactly one stream. Live values stay on dashboards. Monthly reports quote with a timestamp and link to the dashboard. Reports are time capsules. Live numbers stay on the dashboard.\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-gray-300 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Exposed AI services count lives on the Exposure Prevalence Index (ARIAscout).\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Honeypot fleet event totals live on the Attack Prevalence Index (ARIAtrap).\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Sophistication distribution lives on the Sophistication Index (ARIAtrap, distribution-only).\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"HoneyMap surface counts live on the wild-bait dashboard.\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Each Agent Threat Matrix technique resolves to exactly one T-NNNN identifier.\"}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"id\":\"evidence-standards\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Evidence standards\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Every Agent Threat Matrix technique cited in a report carries an evidence tier. We do not publish a technique that does not pass at least one tier. The tier rubric comes from the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://threats.opena2a.org\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Agent Threat Matrix\"}],\" \",\"evidence audit.\"]}],[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-full bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg rw-table-stack\",\"data-label-look\":\"body-white\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"border-b border-gray-800\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left p-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Tier\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left p-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Definition\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"text-right p-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":[\"Count of \",61,\" techniques\"]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tier:observed\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-gray-800/60\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 font-mono\",\"children\":\"OBSERVED\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"data-label\":\"Definition\",\"className\":\"p-3\",\"children\":\"Confirmed in real-world production systems. ARIAscout exposure sweeps, npm supply-chain attacks, real CVE disclosures.\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"data-label\":\"Count of 61 techniques\",\"className\":\"p-3 text-right font-mono text-white\",\"children\":16}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tier:validated\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-gray-800/60\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 font-mono\",\"children\":\"VALIDATED\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"data-label\":\"Definition\",\"className\":\"p-3\",\"children\":\"Reproducible in a controlled lab environment. DVAA challenge fixtures, HMA scan results, sandboxed ARIAred PoCs.\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"data-label\":\"Count of 61 techniques\",\"className\":\"p-3 text-right font-mono text-white\",\"children\":42}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"tier:adapted\",{\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-3 font-mono\",\"children\":\"ADAPTED\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"data-label\":\"Definition\",\"className\":\"p-3\",\"children\":\"A well-understood traditional technique applied to the agent context, with a clear attack vector but no agent-specific observation or lab reproduction yet. Labelled as such on the technique page.\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"data-label\":\"Count of 61 techniques\",\"className\":\"p-3 text-right font-mono text-white\",\"children\":3}]]}]]}]]}]}],null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm\",\"children\":[\"Read from the Threat Matrix catalogue on\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-11-07\",\"children\":\"2026-11-07\"}],\", not typed by hand. The Threat Matrix grows continuously, so this table changes when the catalogue does. The live evidence audit lives at the matrix repository.\"]}]]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12 scroll-mt-20\",\"id\":\"publication-floor\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Publication floor\"}],[[\"$\",\"p\",\"A row in a breakdown, such as events by country, by cloud provider or by ATT\u0026CK ID, is published only when ten or more distinct client addresses are behind it.\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":\"A row in a breakdown, such as events by country, by cloud provider or by ATT\u0026CK ID, is published only when ten or more distinct client addresses are behind it.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"The floor counts addresses, not events or sessions. One address can send thousands of events, so an event or session count never stands in for an address count.\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":\"The floor counts addresses, not events or sessions. One address can send thousands of events, so an event or session count never stands in for an address count.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"A row with fewer addresses behind it can describe one source rather than a pattern across sources.\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":\"A row with fewer addresses behind it can describe one source rather than a pattern across sources.\"}]],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm mb-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"Live TrapMyAgent figures on the threat landscape page.\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Live TrapMyAgent figures on the threat landscape page.\"}],\" \",\"Event types and session classifications are shown only when the sensors report that they applied the floor before publishing them. A row in any other breakdown is shown only when it carries its own count of distinct client addresses at or above the floor. Breakdowns whose rows carry no address count, such as events by country or by cloud provider, cannot be checked against the floor and are withheld.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Dated report editions.\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Dated report editions.\"}],\" \",\"A row in an edition's breakdowns is published only with a recorded count of its distinct client addresses at or above the floor. Until that count is on record, the breakdown is withheld.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm\",\"children\":\"A breakdown that cannot be checked against the floor is not drawn as an empty chart. The page names it once, in a block headed \\\"Breakdowns withheld\\\".\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Per-source limitations\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Every stream has a structural limit. We publish each limit alongside the finding it constrains.\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"HoneyMap is a sample, not a coverage count.\"}],\" Numbers are what CommonCrawl, Shodan banner data, and CT-log domain expansion reached during the reporting window. Surfaces that block crawlers are systematically invisible.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"TrapMyAgent geography reflects origin IP geolocation.\"}],\" VPN, proxy, and Cloudflare-fronting infrastructure can obscure the real origin. ASN-level analysis separates origin from terminus when needed.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"AgentPwn publishes callback counts and a callback share, not an attack-success rate.\"}],\" A callback is a fetch of a canary URL planted in a payload. It does not establish that an agent, rather than a browser, crawler, or scripted client, made the fetch, and it does not measure what the client did next. The callback share is the share of all recorded interactions that were such fetches, a mix descriptor. Per-sector, per-method, and per-family rates are withheld as not measurable. Reports that extrapolate from callbacks to compromise scope should be read with that caveat.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Sophistication scoring is distribution-only.\"}],\" The supervised classifier that would ground a mean does not yet exist. We do not publish a sophistication mean, grade, or month-over-month delta. We publish the per-session distribution and label the rubric as in calibration.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"User-agent strings are not identity claims.\"}],\" Attacker UA strings are attacker-controllable. We report aggregate UA categories with explicit limits, never name a vendor or model without evidence beyond the UA string.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"ARIAscout sees what Shodan indexes.\"}],\" \",\"Shodan's index is a public snapshot of internet-facing infrastructure with banner-grabbing limitations and indexing lag. Services that block Shodan crawlers, run on non-standard ports without service signatures, or sit behind login walls are systematically invisible.\"]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1d:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"How to cite OpenA2A research\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Every report carries a citation block in BibTeX and APA format. Citation makes the work compound. Make citation easy.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded p-4 font-mono text-xs mb-3 overflow-x-auto\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"# BibTeX, generic form\"}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white whitespace-pre-wrap rw-code-wrap\",\"children\":\"@techreport{opena2a-btr-YYYY-MM,\\n  author = {{ARIA, OpenA2A autonomous research system} and \u003ceditor name\u003e (editor)},\\n  title  = {State of AI Agent Security: \u003cMonth\u003e \u003cYear\u003e},\\n  institution = {OpenA2A Research},\\n  year   = {\u003cyear\u003e},\\n  month  = {\u003cmonth\u003e},\\n  type   = {Behavioral Threat Report},\\n  number = {Issue N},\\n  url    = {\u003creport URL\u003e}\\n}\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded p-4 font-mono text-xs mb-3 overflow-x-auto\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"# APA, generic form\"}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white whitespace-pre-wrap rw-code-wrap\",\"children\":\"ARIA, \u0026 \u003cEditor\u003e. (Ed.). (\u003cyear\u003e, \u003cmonth\u003e \u003cday\u003e). State of AI Agent Security: \u003cMonth\u003e \u003cYear\u003e (Behavioral Threat Report Issue N). OpenA2A Research. \u003cURL\u003e\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm\",\"children\":\"DOI assignment is on the roadmap. Until then, the canonical URL of each report is the persistent identifier.\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1e:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"How to challenge a finding\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":[\"Email\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:[email withheld by Lighthouse]\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"[email withheld by Lighthouse]\"}],\" \",\"with the specific number you dispute and the methodology you would prefer we used. Substantive challenges that hold up under review are published as methodology updates in subsequent editions with attribution.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm\",\"children\":[\"Response target: five business days. Disputes that turn on definitions (what counts as an agent, what counts as a session) typically resolve faster than disputes that turn on sampling. We do not maintain a site-wide errata register or a corrections changelog.\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-08\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Issue 4 of the Behavioral Threat Report\"}],\" \",\"re-measures earlier readings against the queries that produced them and publishes both.\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"id\":\"ariascout-exposure-sweep\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"ARIAscout: exposure sweeps\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"ARIAscout is the longest-running stream. It uses \",207,\" Shodan search queries across ten categories to identify internet-facing AI agent infrastructure. The newest reading, with its sweep date, is on the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/indices/exposure-prevalence\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Exposure Prevalence Index\"}],\", which also lists one point per month, each dated to the day it was measured. Sweeps with a written report are in the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/reports/exposure-sweeps\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"exposure sweep archive\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"How a category count is defined.\"}],\" Each category is the sum of every query in it, not a single representative query. The OpenClaw category, for example, is the total across all nine of its queries and not the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"port:18789\"}],\" query on its own, which runs about 1 to 2 percent lower. Issues 1 and 2 of the Behavioral Threat Report published the single-query figure for OpenClaw and Issues 3 and 4 published the category total. Both are real measurements of the sweeps they name, but they are not the same quantity, so a reader comparing an OpenClaw figure across those editions is comparing two definitions. Issue 3's month-over-month sentence has been corrected to use the category total on both sides; the earlier editions stand as published.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Sweep dates are UTC.\"}],\" A sweep is dated by the UTC day it ran, which is the day the canonical store records. A sweep run in the evening in North America therefore carries the following day's date. The April 2026 sweep ran at 02:38 UTC on the 11th and was published on the 10th local; it is dated 2026-04-11 throughout, and the publication date on that report remains the day it was published.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-4 mb-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":\"Key principle\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":\"All findings are based on publicly indexed data and open source code review. We analyze what Shodan has already indexed. We do not access, test, or exploit third-party systems.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-4 mb-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":\"How a sweep is dated and counted\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":[\"A sweep measures one day, not one month. When a later sweep returns a different figure, it supersedes the earlier reading rather than correcting it, and both readings stand: each was accurate on the day it ran. Supersession by a later measurement is therefore not a correction. We use that word for a figure that was wrong when we published it and has a right value to replace it, and withdrawal for one that was wrong and has none. The exposure trend plots one point per month, the latest sweep in that month, and every point carries the day it was measured. The most recent sweep, dated\",\" \",\"$L29\",\", is the plotted endpoint.\"]}],\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\"]}],\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\",\"$L2f\",\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"20:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Reproducibility\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":\"All ARIA methodology is documented for transparency. Each stream's reproduction requirements are published on its sub-page. ARIAscout's requirements:\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"# Requirements\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"- Shodan API key (Freelancer plan for 1000 results per query)\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"- Node.js 18+\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-400 mt-4 mb-2\",\"children\":\"# Analysis parameters\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":[\"- \",207,\" Shodan queries across 10 categories\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"- 6 second delay between Shodan API calls\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"- Banner and header pattern matching for service identification\"}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"21:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-4 text-white\",\"children\":\"Ethics and legal framework\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-gray-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"ARIAscout research is based on analysis of Shodan's publicly available index data.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"ARIAtrap honey agents and AgentPwn honeypot pages run on infrastructure OpenA2A controls.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"HoneyMap samples public-web content via CommonCrawl, Shodan, and CT logs. It does not authenticate into any system.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"No authentication mechanisms on third-party systems are bypassed or tested.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"No private data is retrieved, stored, or disclosed.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"Reports use aggregate statistics only. No organizations, IPs, or domains are identified in published output.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"Security patterns are identified through open source code review and default configuration analysis.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-teal-300\",\"children\":\"*\"}],\"Vulnerability findings flow through the ARIAdesk 90-day coordinated disclosure pipeline before publication.\"]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"22:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-white\",\"children\":\"Questions or concerns?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Questions about methodology or data quality, and coordinated disclosure inquiries, go to\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:[email withheld by Lighthouse]\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"[email withheld by Lighthouse]\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/opena2a-org\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-teal-300 hover:underline\",\"children\":\"Open an issue on GitHub\"}]}]]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$27\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@35\"}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"29:[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-11-01\",\"children\":\"Nov 1, 2026\"}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300 mb-3\",\"children\":[\"Where a month holds more than one sweep, we publish how many it holds and the range they returned, because that range can be wider than the change between months. June 2026 is the clearest case: three sweeps on the same query set returned 349,424 on\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-06-01\",\"children\":\"June 1\"}],\", 320,506 on\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-06-14\",\"children\":\"June 14\"}],\", and 245,111 on\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-06-26\",\"children\":\"June 26\"}],\". The plotted June point is 245,111. The 320,506 reading quoted in the June report remains correct as a measurement of June 14.\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-gray-300\",\"children\":[\"Exposed services and exposed credentials are counted separately, and the boundary is dated. From\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-06-18\",\"children\":\"June 18, 2026\"}],\" the published exposed-services figure excludes the credential categories; sweeps before that date included them. A reader reconstructing a recent figure by summing our per-query totals will therefore land slightly above the published number, by exactly the credential count: the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"time\",null,{\"dateTime\":\"2026-06-26\",\"children\":\"June 26\"}],\" sweep sums to 245,113 against a published 245,111. No previously published figure has been restated onto the newer definition. The difference across the affected sweeps is one to four detections in roughly 300,000, and restating a measurement to match a later definition would replace what we measured with what we derived.\"]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":\"Process\"}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm list-decimal pl-6 mb-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Target discovery via Shodan.\"}],\" \",207,\" queries across Python frameworks, Node.js servers, Go/Java/Ruby/Rust frameworks, cloud platforms, API patterns, AI/ML infrastructure, and agent-framework signatures.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Banner and response analysis.\"}],\" \",\"Shodan's cached banner data and HTTP response headers are analyzed for security-relevant patterns: exposed configuration files, agent instruction files, API key patterns, MCP tool definitions, gateway signatures, and debug mode indicators. Only findings with clear signature matches in the indexed data are counted.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white\",\"children\":\"Aggregation and reporting.\"}],\" Findings are aggregated by pattern type. Rates are computed against the proportion of indexed hosts showing security-relevant patterns. No individual hosts, IPs, or organizations are identified in published output.\"]}]]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white mb-2\",\"children\":\"Shodan query categories\"}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3\",\"children\":[207,\" queries are distributed across these categories.\"]}]\n"])</script><scrip